The pinned finite construction, annealed modules, physical schedules and
terminal-sink integration are eumemic's PR168 work with Anthropic Claude
assistance. The terminal-sink substitution is due to jamesyc (PR166).
The local graph, decoder, shared-core ledger and finite bridge build on
icekylinx (PR144), eumemic (PR117), and Zhihao Chen/Swapnil Jain (PR97).
The late-read conventions build on jamesyc (PR124) and eumemic (PR143).

The new pure exact arithmetic implementations were developed and reviewed
by separate AI agents in this contribution. The scalar event specification
follows the pinned native schedule, while formal variables replace sampled
dirty values. No independent human review or general phase theorem is claimed.
The paired-bit exhaustive-basis approach also follows the separately credited
finite verification approach in huxint's PR170.

The 64 operation-frame refinement is Rohan Arun's PR178 contribution,
prepared with OpenAI Codex assistance, on eumemic's PR168 construction.
PR178 retains PR176's terminal audit technique credited to Chafik Boukhalfa.
Our contribution adds independent exact checks and parameter refinement;
the prerequisite frame construction and all its notices are preserved.
